# Trivy findings dismissed on purpose. Each entry needs a reason; review when the deployment changes.

# KSV-0011 "CPU not limited": deliberate. CPU limits cause throttling under bursts; we set CPU *requests* (for
# scheduling) and memory *limits* (for safety), the commonly recommended pattern.
KSV-0011

# KSV-01010 "ConfigMap with sensitive content": false positive. The rule matches the key name LOG_LEVEL; the
# ConfigMap holds only ENVIRONMENT, LOG_LEVEL and CORS_ORIGINS. Secrets come from Secret objects.
KSV-01010
